IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`
IMPORT `P8-art73`

-- P8-art75: Article 75, market surveillance and control of AI systems and mutual assistance (the AI Office). LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). The Omnibus REPLACED the title and paragraph 1 and INSERTED paragraphs 1a to 1e and 2a (the `▼M1` passages);
-- paragraphs 2 and 3 are as enacted (`▼B`). Paragraph 1 is encoded in both versions, each in its own function (the as-enacted branch is dead through the dispatcher,
-- because the group applies from 2 August 2026 and the amended text from 27 July 2026); the inserted paragraphs have only the amended version.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 75 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 75(1a) report the serious incident to the AI Office`
    `Art 75(1a) transmit the relevant information promptly to the market surveillance authority of the Member State`
    `Art 75(1b) cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the necessary assistance`
    `Art 75(1c) assist the AI Office in the investigatory or enforcement action`
    `Art 75(1d) notify the market surveillance authority competent for the market of the intention to take the decision`
    `Art 75(1d) consult the authorities involved in the application of this Regulation`
    `Art 75(1e) pay the costs related to the services entrusted to the notified body directly to the notified body`
    `Art 75(2) cooperate with the AI Office to carry out compliance evaluations`
    `Art 75(2) inform the Board and the other market surveillance authorities`
    `Art 75(2a) cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the necessary assistance`
    `Art 75(2a) inform the single point of contact of the AI Office's intention to exercise its powers or of its reasons for not exercising them`
    `Art 75(2a) inform the single point of contact periodically about major developments and the outcome of the proceedings`
    `Art 75(3) supply to the applicant authority the information that the AI Office considers relevant`
    `Art 75(3) safeguard the confidentiality of the information obtained in accordance with Article 78`

§ `Article 75(1): the AI Office's competence (replaced by the Omnibus)`

-- VERSION as enacted. "Where an AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model, and the model and the system are developed by the same provider, the AI Office
-- shall have powers to monitor and supervise compliance of that AI system with obligations under this Regulation."
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1773 | 1. Where an AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model, and the model and the system are developed by the same provider, the AI Office shall have powers to monitor and supervise compliance of that AI system with obligations under this Regulation. To carry out its monitoring and supervision tasks, the AI Office shall have all the powers of a market surveillance authority provided for in this Section and Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.
@ref Art 75(1) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1773)
GIVEN `the AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model and the system are developed by the same provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1) as enacted the AI Office has powers to monitor and supervise compliance of the AI system with obligations under this Regulation` MEANS
    IF `the AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model` AND `the model and the system are developed by the same provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model, and the model and the system are developed by the same provider" (a power gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-75-1-where)

-- VERSION as amended, point (a): the exclusive competence over AI systems based on general-purpose AI models developed by the same provider (or undertaking),
-- "with the exception of" four kinds of system.
-- src:1170 | 1. The AI Office shall be exclusively competent for the supervision and enforcement of the obligations under this Regulation in relation to the following AI systems:
-- src:1171 | (a) AI systems based on general-purpose AI models where the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider, with the exception of:
-- src:1172 | (i) AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;
-- src:1173 | (ii) AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III;
-- src:1174 | (iii) AI systems provided by law enforcement authorities, border management authorities and financial institutions, insofar as those AI systems fall under Article 74(6); and
-- src:1175 | (iv) AI systems referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice;
@ref Art 75(1) first subparagraph point (a) and (a)(i) to (iv) as amended (src:1170-1175)
GIVEN `the AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is provided by a law enforcement authority, a border management authority or a financial institution, in so far as it falls under Article 74(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1)(a) as amended the AI Office is exclusively competent for the AI system based on a general-purpose AI model` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model` AND `the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (a) reaches "AI systems based on general-purpose AI models where the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking"
    ELSE IF     `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I`
             OR `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III`
             OR `the AI system is provided by a law enforcement authority, a border management authority or a financial institution, in so far as it falls under Article 74(6)`
             OR `the AI system is referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the exception of: (i) AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I; (ii) ... point 2 of Annex III; (iii) ... Article 74(6); and (iv) ... point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1176 | (b) AI systems that constitute or that are integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.
@ref Art 75(1) first subparagraph point (b) as amended (src:1176)
GIVEN `the AI system constitutes or is integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1)(b) as amended the AI Office is exclusively competent for the AI system that is or is integrated into a very large online platform or search engine` MEANS
    IF `the AI system constitutes or is integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (b) reaches AI systems that constitute or are integrated into a very large online platform or search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065

-- Points (a) and (b) together. The list of systems is introduced by "the following" and not closed with "only": a system in neither point is not covered.
-- src:1170 | 1. The AI Office shall be exclusively competent for the supervision and enforcement of the obligations under this Regulation in relation to the following AI systems:
-- src:1171 | (a) AI systems based on general-purpose AI models where the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider, with the exception of:
-- src:1172 | (i) AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;
-- src:1173 | (ii) AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III;
-- src:1174 | (iii) AI systems provided by law enforcement authorities, border management authorities and financial institutions, insofar as those AI systems fall under Article 74(6); and
-- src:1175 | (iv) AI systems referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice;
-- src:1176 | (b) AI systems that constitute or that are integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.
@ref Art 75(1) first subparagraph as amended (src:1170-1176)
GIVEN `the AI Office is exclusively competent under point (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the AI Office is exclusively competent under point (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1) first subparagraph as amended the AI Office is exclusively competent for the AI system` MEANS
    IF `the AI Office is exclusively competent under point (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the AI Office is exclusively competent under point (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the AI Office is exclusively competent under point (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the exception of" (the exception of point (a) holds and point (b) does not)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the systems of points (a) and (b) are listed without "only"

-- Second subparagraph: to whom the exclusive competence applies.
-- src:1177 | The exclusive competence referred to in the first subparagraph shall apply to the providers of those systems. It shall apply to the deployers of those systems only when they are also the provider or form part of the same undertaking as the provider.
@ref Art 75(1) second subparagraph as amended (src:1177)
GIVEN `the party is a provider of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is a deployer of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer is also the provider or forms part of the same undertaking as the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1) second subparagraph as amended the exclusive competence of the AI Office applies to the party` MEANS
    IF `the party is a provider of the AI system`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- "The exclusive competence referred to in the first subparagraph shall apply to the providers of those systems"
    ELSE IF `the party is a deployer of the AI system`
         THEN IF `the deployer is also the provider or forms part of the same undertaking as the provider`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It shall apply to the deployers of those systems only when they are also the provider or form part of the same undertaking as the provider"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks of providers and deployers only

-- The dispatcher: the group's gate, then the version in force. The facts of both versions are asked; the as-enacted branch is dead (NOTES.md).
-- src:1170 | 1. The AI Office shall be exclusively competent for the supervision and enforcement of the obligations under this Regulation in relation to the following AI systems:
-- src:1171 | (a) AI systems based on general-purpose AI models where the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider, with the exception of:
-- src:1172 | (i) AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;
-- src:1173 | (ii) AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III;
-- src:1174 | (iii) AI systems provided by law enforcement authorities, border management authorities and financial institutions, insofar as those AI systems fall under Article 74(6); and
-- src:1175 | (iv) AI systems referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice;
-- src:1176 | (b) AI systems that constitute or that are integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.
-- src:1177 | The exclusive competence referred to in the first subparagraph shall apply to the providers of those systems. It shall apply to the deployers of those systems only when they are also the provider or form part of the same undertaking as the provider.
@ref Art 75(1), both versions (src:1170-1177)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is provided by a law enforcement authority, a border management authority or a financial institution, in so far as it falls under Article 74(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system constitutes or is integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1) the AI Office is competent for the supervision and enforcement of the obligations in relation to the AI system` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 75(1) as enacted the AI Office has powers to monitor and supervise compliance of the AI system with obligations under this Regulation` `the AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model` `the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN  -- VERSION as amended
             `Art 75(1) first subparagraph as amended the AI Office is exclusively competent for the AI system` (`Art 75(1)(a) as amended the AI Office is exclusively competent for the AI system based on a general-purpose AI model` `the AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model` `the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider` `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III` `the AI system is provided by a law enforcement authority, a border management authority or a financial institution, in so far as it falls under Article 74(6)` `the AI system is referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice`) (`Art 75(1)(b) as amended the AI Office is exclusively competent for the AI system that is or is integrated into a very large online platform or search engine` `the AI system constitutes or is integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065`)

§ `Article 75(1a): serious incidents of systems under the AI Office (inserted by the Omnibus)`

-- src:1179 | 1a. By way of derogation from Article 73, providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article shall report any serious incidents to the AI Office. Article 73 (2) to (9), shall apply mutatis mutandis. The AI Office shall promptly transmit the relevant information to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the provider or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75(1a) first sentence (src:1179)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event is a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1a) first sentence the provider must report the serious incident to the AI Office` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 75 1
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision speaks of high-risk AI systems
              ELSE IF `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1` AND `the event is a serious incident`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is a scope limit with no "only": "providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article shall report any serious incidents to the AI Office" (ruling (c); fork F-75-1a-scope states the other reading)

-- src:1179 | 1a. By way of derogation from Article 73, providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article shall report any serious incidents to the AI Office. Article 73 (2) to (9), shall apply mutatis mutandis. The AI Office shall promptly transmit the relevant information to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the provider or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75(1a) second sentence (src:1179)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the provider or, where applicable, the deployer becomes aware of the serious incident` IS A DATE
      `the event is a widespread infringement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event is a serious incident as defined in Article 3, point (49)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event is the death of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75 act`
`Art 75(1a) the provider's duty to report the serious incident to the AI Office` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 75 1
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1`
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed to the AI Office: the first sentence is for "providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1" (Article 73 governs the others)
         ELSE CONSIDER `Art 73(2) to (4) the number of days after becoming aware within which the report must be made` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the event is a widespread infringement` `the event is a serious incident as defined in Article 3, point (49)(b)` `the event is the death of a person`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked, the system is saved by Art 111(2), or the system is not high-risk
             WHEN JUST `the days` THEN  -- "Article 73 (2) to (9), shall apply mutatis mutandis": the periods of Art 73(2), (3) and (4) are the same
                 PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party provider`
                 MUST `Art 75(1a) report the serious incident to the AI Office`
                 WITHIN (Day (`the date the provider or, where applicable, the deployer becomes aware of the serious incident` PLUS `the days`)) MINUS (Day `the date the provider or, where applicable, the deployer becomes aware of the serious incident`)
                 HENCE FULFILLED
                 LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party provider` BECAUSE "the serious incident was not reported to the AI Office within the period Article 73(2), (3) or (4) gives"

-- src:1179 | 1a. By way of derogation from Article 73, providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article shall report any serious incidents to the AI Office. Article 73 (2) to (9), shall apply mutatis mutandis. The AI Office shall promptly transmit the relevant information to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the provider or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75(1a) third sentence (src:1179)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has received a report of a serious incident under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1a) third sentence the AI Office must promptly transmit the relevant information to the market surveillance authority of the Member State` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI Office has received a report of a serious incident under this paragraph`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The AI Office shall promptly transmit the relevant information" (it arises upon a report under this paragraph) (fork F-75-1a-third-duty)

-- src:1179 | 1a. By way of derogation from Article 73, providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article shall report any serious incidents to the AI Office. Article 73 (2) to (9), shall apply mutatis mutandis. The AI Office shall promptly transmit the relevant information to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the provider or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75(1a) third sentence (src:1179)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has received a report of a serious incident under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75 act`
`Art 75(1a) third sentence the AI Office's duty to transmit the relevant information promptly` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the AI Office has received a report of a serious incident under this paragraph`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked, or no report has been received
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MUST `Art 75(1a) transmit the relevant information promptly to the market surveillance authority of the Member State`
        HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 75(1b) to (1d): cooperation, assistance, notice before a decision`

-- src:1180 | 1b. The authorities involved in the application of this Regulation shall cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the AI Office the necessary assistance for the exercise of its powers, including, where necessary, in connection with inspections or other enforcement measures carried out in the territory of a Member State. To that end, those authorities shall enjoy the powers provided for pursuant to this Regulation and Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, and where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks under this paragraph, in accordance with the applicable national procedures.
@ref Art 75(1b) first sentence (src:1180)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1b) first sentence the authorities involved in the application of this Regulation must cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the necessary assistance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "shall cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the AI Office the necessary assistance"

-- src:1180 | 1b. The authorities involved in the application of this Regulation shall cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the AI Office the necessary assistance for the exercise of its powers, including, where necessary, in connection with inspections or other enforcement measures carried out in the territory of a Member State. To that end, those authorities shall enjoy the powers provided for pursuant to this Regulation and Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, and where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks under this paragraph, in accordance with the applicable national procedures.
@ref Art 75(1b) first sentence (src:1180)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75 act`
`Art 75(1b) the authorities' duty to cooperate actively with the AI Office` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party national competent authority`
        MUST `Art 75(1b) cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the necessary assistance`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1180 | 1b. The authorities involved in the application of this Regulation shall cooperate actively with the AI Office and provide the AI Office the necessary assistance for the exercise of its powers, including, where necessary, in connection with inspections or other enforcement measures carried out in the territory of a Member State. To that end, those authorities shall enjoy the powers provided for pursuant to this Regulation and Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, and where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks under this paragraph, in accordance with the applicable national procedures.
@ref Art 75(1b) second sentence (src:1180)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the powers are relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the powers are limited to what is necessary to fulfil the authorities' tasks under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the powers are exercised in accordance with the applicable national procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1b) second sentence the authorities enjoy the powers provided for pursuant to this Regulation and Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the powers are relevant` AND `the powers are limited to what is necessary to fulfil the authorities' tasks under this paragraph` AND `the powers are exercised in accordance with the applicable national procedures`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks under this paragraph, in accordance with the applicable national procedures" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b))

-- src:1181 | 1c. When taking investigatory or enforcement action in the territory of a Member State that involves access to a public authority’s data or AI system, the AI Office shall be assisted by the relevant market surveillance authority.
@ref Art 75(1c) (src:1181)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office takes investigatory or enforcement action in the territory of a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action involves access to a public authority's data or AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1c) the relevant market surveillance authority must assist the AI Office` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI Office takes investigatory or enforcement action in the territory of a Member State` AND `the action involves access to a public authority's data or AI system`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When taking investigatory or enforcement action in the territory of a Member State that involves access to a public authority's data or AI system" (an unmet "when" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) (fork F-75-1c-duty)

-- src:1181 | 1c. When taking investigatory or enforcement action in the territory of a Member State that involves access to a public authority’s data or AI system, the AI Office shall be assisted by the relevant market surveillance authority.
@ref Art 75(1c) (src:1181)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the action involves access to a public authority's data or AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75 act`
`Art 75(1c) the market surveillance authority's duty to assist the AI Office` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the action involves access to a public authority's data or AI system`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked, or the action does not involve access to a public authority's data or AI system
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 75(1c) assist the AI Office in the investigatory or enforcement action`
        HENCE FULFILLED

