§ `Article 75(1e): conformity assessments by the AI Office and fees`

-- src:1183 | 1e. The AI Office shall be responsible for conformity assessments and tests of AI systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article that are classified as high-risk and subject to a third-party conformity assessment pursuant to Article 43 before such AI systems are placed on the market or put into service. Those tests and assessments shall verify that the systems comply with the relevant requirements of this Regulation and may be placed on the market or put into service in the Union in accordance with this Regulation. The Commission shall entrust the performance of those tests or assessments to notified bodies designated in accordance with this Regulation, in which case the notified body shall act on behalf of the Commission. If a notified body to which the Commission has delegated tasks under this paragraph does not perform those tasks adequately, the Commission may withdraw the delegation with immediate effect.
@ref Art 75(1e) first sentence (src:1183)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is classified as high-risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is subject to a third-party conformity assessment pursuant to Article 43` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment and tests are before the AI system is placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1e) first sentence the AI Office is responsible for the conformity assessments and tests of the AI system` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 75 1
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF `the AI system is referred to in paragraph 1` AND `the AI system is classified as high-risk` AND `the AI system is subject to a third-party conformity assessment pursuant to Article 43` AND `the assessment and tests are before the AI system is placed on the market or put into service`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is limited to the case its own words describe; the text is silent on the other cases

