§ `Article 75(3): access to information about the general-purpose AI model`

-- src:1195 | 3. Where a market surveillance authority is unable to conclude its investigation of the high-risk AI system because of its inability to access certain information related to the general-purpose AI model despite having made all appropriate efforts to obtain that information, it may submit a reasoned request to the AI Office, by which access to that information shall be enforced. In that case, the AI Office shall supply to the applicant authority without delay, and in any event within 30 days, any information that the AI Office considers to be relevant in order to establish whether a high-risk AI system is non-compliant. Market surveillance authorities shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain in accordance with Article 78 of this Regulation. The procedure provided for in Chapter VI of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis.
@ref Art 75(3) first sentence (src:1195)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority is unable to conclude its investigation of the high-risk AI system because of its inability to access certain information related to the general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has made all appropriate efforts to obtain that information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(3) first sentence the market surveillance authority may submit a reasoned request to the AI Office by which access to the information is enforced` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the market surveillance authority is unable to conclude its investigation of the high-risk AI system because of its inability to access certain information related to the general-purpose AI model` AND `the authority has made all appropriate efforts to obtain that information`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a market surveillance authority is unable to conclude its investigation ... despite having made all appropriate efforts to obtain that information, it may submit a reasoned request" (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-75-3-where)

-- src:1195 | 3. Where a market surveillance authority is unable to conclude its investigation of the high-risk AI system because of its inability to access certain information related to the general-purpose AI model despite having made all appropriate efforts to obtain that information, it may submit a reasoned request to the AI Office, by which access to that information shall be enforced. In that case, the AI Office shall supply to the applicant authority without delay, and in any event within 30 days, any information that the AI Office considers to be relevant in order to establish whether a high-risk AI system is non-compliant. Market surveillance authorities shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain in accordance with Article 78 of this Regulation. The procedure provided for in Chapter VI of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis.
@ref Art 75(3) second sentence (src:1195)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI Office received the reasoned request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 75(3) second sentence the date by which the AI Office must supply the information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST (`the date the AI Office received the reasoned request` PLUS 30)  -- "without delay, and in any event within 30 days"

-- src:1195 | 3. Where a market surveillance authority is unable to conclude its investigation of the high-risk AI system because of its inability to access certain information related to the general-purpose AI model despite having made all appropriate efforts to obtain that information, it may submit a reasoned request to the AI Office, by which access to that information shall be enforced. In that case, the AI Office shall supply to the applicant authority without delay, and in any event within 30 days, any information that the AI Office considers to be relevant in order to establish whether a high-risk AI system is non-compliant. Market surveillance authorities shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain in accordance with Article 78 of this Regulation. The procedure provided for in Chapter VI of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis.
@ref Art 75(3) second sentence (src:1195)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75 act`
`Art 75(3) second sentence the AI Office's duty to supply the information within 30 days` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MUST `Art 75(3) supply to the applicant authority the information that the AI Office considers relevant`
        WITHIN 30
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office` BECAUSE "the information was not supplied to the applicant authority within 30 days of the request"

